{
  "name": "life_story_world_record",
  "description": "Record the author and the world before the story, one stage at a time: author_reader (the author's life as its own life model, in whatever structure understands them best, whose open questions this stage returns; the voice; why they write this story, what they want to teach and what they are figuring out, citing the life records; optionally an example reader's life the same way; and the buttons the story presses in its reader), candidates (at least three candidate worlds that come out of the author's life and press those buttons, with premise, emotional core, long-term processes, principals and pressure tests, and a selection with reasons), opening (successive expansions of the chosen world), aspects (every aspect of the story one could understand better, from the characters' choices and the author's style to the technology and the period, each investigated by modeling), implications (each commitment's consequences traced to model records or reasoned remainder) and route (the parts to render, each with Events, focal route and change, found where the model jumps). Record them in any order, whenever the understanding happens, and revise any of them when the model leads back; each is validated against the life models and the bound model and against whichever related stages exist, stored as an author record, and returns the model's open questions. Scene preparation shows what the world holds and what is still open. Use the model for all of it. Investigate who the author is, and who the book is for (stage author_reader). Investigate which worlds this author could write, and choose one by argument (candidates). Investigate the chosen world, opening it in successive accounts (opening). Investigate everything that makes this story interesting, the returned catalog as a start (aspects). Investigate what each commitment implies (implications). Investigate where in the model the story is (route). Ask whether the author lives in this world or a separate one; if in this one, when they write the book matters. Their life can be a model of its own or a realm of the story's, and notes can link records of any stored model, so hold what the author lived together with what it shapes. These come in any order and again whenever the model leads back to them; record each with life_story_world_record when the understanding happens, let the director (life_story_direct) hold the world and the draft to what makes a story good, and write each scene from the model's state at its moment. Add-only: graphHash may be any earlier revision of the story graph; the record goes to its newest head, and advancedFrom says so.\n\nRespect the human author's starting brief and chosen involvement. For a new story, ask about unresolved initial settings and writing-process involvement separately; reuse explicit preferences and delegation. Offer setting all or some parameters or delegating them, and autonomous work, selected checkpoints, ongoing collaboration, or a custom arrangement. Read life-sim://addon/storytelling for intake guidance. Automatic modeling and reviews operate within that agreement. Wait for the human at agreed approval checkpoints; saving a proposal or passing a review is not their approval. A bounded review or edit request does not require a new-project questionnaire.",
  "inputSchema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "graphHash": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[a-f0-9]{64}$"
      },
      "requestId": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1,
        "maxLength": 256
      },
      "nodeId": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1,
        "maxLength": 256
      },
      "storyRootId": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1,
        "maxLength": 256
      },
      "authorId": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1,
        "maxLength": 256
      },
      "exactRevision": {
        "default": false,
        "description": "Write against graphHash exactly, creating a branch if it is not the newest revision. By default an add-only record goes to the newest head.",
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "accessScopes": {
        "minItems": 1,
        "maxItems": 64,
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "maxLength": 256
        }
      },
      "summary": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 10,
        "maxLength": 4000,
        "description": "A few sentences a later reader sees first."
      },
      "world": {
        "oneOf": [
          {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "stage": {
                "type": "string",
                "const": "author_reader"
              },
              "author": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "personId": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "maxLength": 256,
                    "description": "The referent of this person in their life model, compiled from the person template (person_scaffold)."
                  },
                  "name": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "maxLength": 200
                  },
                  "mode": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "enum": [
                      "real",
                      "invented"
                    ],
                    "description": "A real person modeled from supplied or known evidence, or an invented person labelled as invented."
                  },
                  "lifeModelHash": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "pattern": "^[a-f0-9]{64}$",
                    "description": "The model holding the person's life: its own model, or the story's model with the person's reality as a realm of its own (a context root). Either way notes can link to its records: about targets may name records of any stored model."
                  },
                  "authorModelNodeId": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1,
                    "maxLength": 256,
                    "description": "The stored author model (life_story_author_record, kind author_model): the voice this life produces. Its modeledAuthorId is personId."
                  },
                  "livesIn": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "enum": [
                      "this_world",
                      "separate_world"
                    ],
                    "description": "Does the author live in this story's world, or a separate one? A memoir or a story among the author's own people lives in this world; an invented world usually does not."
                  },
                  "writing": {
                    "default": null,
                    "description": "If the author lives in this world: when they write the book relative to the story's events, what they know then, and how far they stand from what they tell. It shapes what can be documented.",
                    "anyOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "string",
                        "minLength": 10,
                        "maxLength": 4000
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "null"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "whyThisStory": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 20,
                    "maxLength": 4000,
                    "description": "Why this person writes this story now, read from their modeled life."
                  },
                  "teach": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 3,
                    "maxLength": 4000,
                    "description": "What they want to teach or show; say so when nothing is settled."
                  },
                  "figuringOut": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 20,
                    "maxLength": 4000,
                    "description": "What they are figuring out by writing it: the question their own conflicting wants leave open."
                  },
                  "lifeRecords": {
                    "minItems": 2,
                    "maxItems": 24,
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "minLength": 3,
                      "maxLength": 1024,
                      "description": "A model record as kind:id (event:ev.x, process:p.x, cut:c.x, referent:r.x, concept:c.x) or a graph node id."
                    },
                    "description": "The records of the author's life model this reasoning rests on (event:, cut:, process:)."
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "personId",
                  "name",
                  "mode",
                  "lifeModelHash",
                  "authorModelNodeId",
                  "livesIn",
                  "whyThisStory",
                  "teach",
                  "figuringOut",
                  "lifeRecords"
                ],
                "additionalProperties": false
              },
              "reader": {
                "default": null,
                "description": "An optional example reader, modeled as a life in the same way.",
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                      "personId": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "minLength": 1,
                        "maxLength": 256,
                        "description": "The referent of this person in their life model, compiled from the person template (person_scaffold)."
                      },
                      "name": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "minLength": 1,
                        "maxLength": 200
                      },
                      "mode": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "enum": [
                          "real",
                          "invented"
                        ],
                        "description": "A real person modeled from supplied or known evidence, or an invented person labelled as invented."
                      },
                      "lifeModelHash": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "pattern": "^[a-f0-9]{64}$",
                        "description": "The model holding the person's life: its own model, or the story's model with the person's reality as a realm of its own (a context root). Either way notes can link to its records: about targets may name records of any stored model."
                      },
                      "situation": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "minLength": 10,
                        "maxLength": 4000,
                        "description": "What is happening in their life when they read this book."
                      }
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "personId",
                      "name",
                      "mode",
                      "lifeModelHash",
                      "situation"
                    ],
                    "additionalProperties": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "buttons": {
                "minItems": 1,
                "maxItems": 8,
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "id": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "minLength": 1,
                      "maxLength": 256
                    },
                    "button": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "minLength": 5,
                      "maxLength": 2000,
